<p>Living in (or close to) a city with phenomenal connectivity is a life goal of mine. These so called “hubs”  are by default cosmopolitian in nature - Talk to any random person in London and you will see they come from nearly everywhere on the globe. Talk to a person in a Gamma- city and they likely are from the city in question.</p>
<p>I believe the reason we in Edmonton for example hate travel so much (talk to a lot of people, they don’t like it, find it a tremendous hassle, or don’t do it altogether) is because of this lack of ability to get where we want to go without issue. Sure it is called the “Edmonton International Airport” but quite frankly, we have to do a much better job before we can really call it “international”.</p>
<p>Maybe you’d make travelling part of your life if you lived somewhere you could just hop on a plane and go?</p>